<title>SPAIN: Spain's Cepsa 1996 net down four percent.</title>
<headline>Spain's Cepsa 1996 net down four percent.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Cepsa ended 1996 with a net profit of 20.85 billion pesetas, down four percent from previous year.</p>
<p> Net taxed			    20.85	 vs	  21.85</p>
<p> Turnover			  1,165.79	 vs     1,055.06</p>
<p> Gross Operating result	   53.77	 vs	  66.35</p>
<p> Dividend total		     10.70	 vs	  10.70</p>
<p> Investments			  59.22	 vs	  51.48</p>
<p> Net fixed assets		  371.56	 vs	 309.84</p>
<p>NOTE - Cepsa paid in October an interim dividend of 60 pesetas and it intends to pay after the shareholders meeting a final dividend of other 60 pesetas to a total of 120 pesetas per share.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
